 R←Test_API_030(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;buff;res;hash1;hash2
⍝ Runs "CompareCommits" on two commits with identical trees. Git then reports no differences at
⍝ all, and <DiffBetween> used to turn that into a RANK ERROR because ¨ was applied to an empty
⍝ vector, which applies the function to the fill element.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 (rc msg buff)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'commit -q --allow-empty -m "Nothing at all"'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 hash1←G.GetLastCommit tempDir
 (rc msg buff)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'rev-parse HEAD~1'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 hash2←∊buff

 res←tempDir G.CompareCommits hash1 hash2
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∧/0=≢¨2↑res              ⍝ Nothing to compare, so no files are left behind

 ⍝ <DiffBetween> itself must return the documented shape, not crash
 buff←tempDir G.DiffBetween hash1 hash2
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠⍴⍴buff
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢buff

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
